# Repo is PRIVATE — Alex chose to keep the MIST voice data in the repo rather
# than gitignore it. We still exclude two categories for practical reasons:

# 1) Big regenerable source: the raw supercut is >100MB (GitHub's hard per-file
#    limit, no LFS here) and is reproducible via yt-dlp. Isolated stems likewise.
samples/raw/
samples/isolated/

# 2) Pretrained PUBLIC model weights (~1.8GB XTTS + whisper) — not our data,
#    redownloaded automatically by the scripts.
models/

# Transient synthesis outputs
out.wav

# Python env
.venv/
__pycache__/

# Kept IN the repo (the irreplaceable curation work):
#   samples/reference/  — the MIST reference clips + _archive of dropped takes
#   demo_mist.wav        — the canonical approved sample
